I've left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and this request would add an outbound HTTP import that the grant doesn't declare. The fetch's result is also discarded, so it does nothing except send untrusted feed text to an external host, and building the URL by string interpolation would let input alter the query. If the platform team wants this, it should go through a graph-level change that adds a scoped `http-client` handle to the `with` clause and encodes the query. The implementation below keeps the node to its declared `state-read` grant.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(item.id.as_str()).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

